# vvaharness environment — copy to .env and fill in.
# vvaharness auto-loads this file (searched from the working directory upward),
# so no manual `source` is needed. Shell-exported vars take precedence. For
# safety, a `.env` located inside the scan target is ignored by default.
#
# The DEFAULT profile is mixed: local S0; Claude CLI for S1-S9; DeepAgents with
# Anthropic for both S10 and S11. A complete default run therefore needs Claude
# Code auth plus Anthropic provider credentials — no OpenAI key is required.
# Missing post-scan credentials cause S10/S11 to be skipped with a warning;
# `--stop-after s9` is detection-only.

# ── Anthropic SDK (primary credential for `via: sdk` roles) ──────────────────
# sdk.yaml S11 does not translate this name; it uses Claude login/OAuth or the
# standard ANTHROPIC_API_KEY / ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN names below. A standard
# credential alone is also accepted as the direct SDK fallback when SDK is the
# profile's only backend.
ANTHROPIC_SDK_API_KEY=

# Optional direct-SDK endpoint. A `via: sdk` Agent-SDK S10 session translates it to
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL; S11 does not. Leave blank for the public API.
ANTHROPIC_SDK_BASE_URL=
# OPTIONAL — CA bundle for a private gateway / TLS-intercepting proxy whose
# server cert chains to an internal root CA. Use an ABSOLUTE path: a relative
# value resolves against the selected YAML profile's directory. Direct SDK
# detection only; Agent-SDK S10/S11 do not consume it. Leave blank publicly.
ANTHROPIC_SDK_CA_CERT=
# OPTIONAL — absolute client-cert path for mutual TLS (mTLS), direct SDK
# detection only. Agent-SDK S10/S11 do not consume it.
ANTHROPIC_SDK_CLIENT_CERT=

# ── DeepAgents + Anthropic (default S10 remediation and S11 validation) ──────
# Set this key or the commented ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN alternative for default
# S10 and S11. For sdk/full S11 either is one option alongside ambient Claude
# login or CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN. Do not set both unless explicitly required.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=
# Gateway users may also need ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL and process-level CA settings.
# See docs/SETUP_GUIDE.md; they are intentionally not blank assignments here.

# ── Claude Code CLI (`via: cli` — default S1-S9) ─────────────────────────────
# Direct CLI roles and sdk/full S11 may use an existing `claude` login or this
# setup token. sdk/full S11 still requires the external `claude` executable.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# OPTIONAL — absolute CA-bundle path for the direct `via: cli` adapter's
# `claude` subprocess (-> NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS). Relative values resolve against
# the selected config's directory. Leave blank to use normal process trust.
CLAUDE_CLI_CA_CERT=

# ── OpenAI / OpenAI-compatible (`via: openai`, or DeepAgents with ────────────
# ── `provider: openai`; not used by any shipped profile) ─────────────────────
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_BASE_URL=
# OPTIONAL — absolute CA-bundle path for the direct `via: openai` client only;
# relative values resolve against the selected config's directory. It is not
# used by a DeepAgents/OpenAI route. Leave blank publicly.
OPENAI_CA_CERT=

# ── Batch cloning (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
GITHUB_TOKEN=
GIT_BASE_URL=
